                                "example_id": "30657bd4-d930-4f85-ab14-2178be5ae6fd",
                                "sense_id": "0226bd09-97ea-3e1e-82c6-1e84dfe91b4b",
                                "text": "We hope it will not be unconsidered, that we finde no open tract, or constant manuduction in this Labyrinth; but are oft-times fain to wander in the America and untravelled parts of Truth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e063434-4f71-4aab-b4ef-0579c2e3b5b1",
                                "sense_id": "0226bd09-97ea-3e1e-82c6-1e84dfe91b4b",
                                "text": "That the Aristotelian Physiology cannot boast it self the proper Author of any one Invention; is prægnant evidence of its infecundous deficiency: And ’twould puzzle the Schools to point at any considerable discovery, made by the direct, sole manuduction of Peripatetick Principles."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
